---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
---

<section class="wrap section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <SectionHeading id="about">About</SectionHeading>

  <div class="prose" data-reveal>
    <p>
      I started out studying Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning at Anurag University in Hyderabad, and I am now
      pursuing my M.S. in Data Science, Analytics and Engineering at Arizona State University.
    </p>
    <p class="pull">What interests me most is the point where AI stops being a model and starts becoming a product.</p>
    <p>
      I like taking an idea all the way from the intelligence behind it to the system someone actually interacts with. With
      Zoom Lens, that means building an AI assistant directly into a meeting so someone can privately understand what is
      being shared without interrupting the conversation. In another project, it meant building a support-ticket model that
      predicts priority and resolution time, then using SHAP to show why it made each prediction.
    </p>
    <p class="pull">But I do not want a system to just look like it works.</p>
    <p>
      I want evidence. I have built ETL pipelines that reconcile millions of records, tested APIs under concurrent requests,
      written ground truth by hand, and measured models against real baselines. I also document the limits of those results,
      whether that is synthetic data, a controlled test environment, or a system that has not yet been tested at production
      scale.
    </p>
    <p>
      That is the work I enjoy: building useful AI, engineering the systems around it, and being able to explain exactly how I
      know they work.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-top: var(--section-gap);
  }

  .prose {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }

  .pull {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
</style>
